<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hezb-e Wahdat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1989</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Hizb-i Wahdat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hezb-e Wahdat is an Afghan political party founded in 1989 as a union of Shia factions representing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hazara">Hazara</a> people, under Abdul Ali Mazari. During the civil war of the 1990s it fought other factions for control of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a>. It later joined the Northern Alliance against the Taliban, which killed Mazari in 1995.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hezb-e-wahdat.jpg" alt="Hezb-e Wahdat" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MrPenguin20 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_Hezbe_Wahdat.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
